      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-213431",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A={1,2,3}.$ \n\n$$\nR={(1,1),(1,2),(1,3),(2,1),(2,3),(3,2),(3,3)}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince \n{{field-1}}\n$\\in R$ and \n{{field-2}}\n$\\in R,$ but \n{{field-3}}\n$\\notin R,$ the relation is\n{{field-4}}."
